== Notes ==
* Although The Haunt can fly over rocks and most other obstacles, its movement in the second phase can be completely stopped by dropping a bomb in its path.
** {{dlc|anr}} In [[Afterbirth]] and [[Afterbirth †]], the Haunt is no longer stopped by bombs and can move over them.
* Lil' Haunts are immune to the effects of {{I|E. Coli}}, {{I|Flush!}}, {{I|D10|nr}} and {{dlc|r}} [[Cards and Runes#Playing Cards|Ace cards]].
* Inflicting [[fear]] or [[confusion]] on The Haunt during Phase 2 can be dangerous, as it will sometimes start sliding back and forth rapidly.
* The Haunt can be damaged in phase 1 using {{I|Dark Arts}} and {{I|The Boomerang}}.
* The Haunt can be instantly killed with {{I|Vade Retro}} if it is at 50% health or below.

== Trivia ==
* It is the boss version of the Lil' Haunts.
* {{e|The Forsaken}} is the posthumous version of it.
* The Haunt's design may be a reference to [[gish:Paunchy Chops|Paunchy Chops]], a boss from the game ''Gish'', also developed by Edmund McMillen. They function similarly in that they are both ghosts that can phase in and out of corporeality, and they bear similar facial expressions.
* {{Dlc|r}} The Haunt has a resurrected variation known as {{e|The Heretic|n}}.
* Black Champion Haunt in its second phase resembles {{c|Tainted Lost}}.

